trip/false/crop/4000x3000+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F75%2Fc3%2Fe8a03c2e40d59ec63338b96ca3d8%2Fnc-tumpak-sewu-s-majestic-waterfall-colas-decloitre.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x3000+0+0/resize/2000/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F75%2Fc3%2Fe8a03c2e40d59ec63338b96ca3d8%2Fnc-tumpak-sewu-s-majestic-waterfall-colas-decloitre.jpg 2000w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x3000+0+0/resize/2600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F75%2Fc3%2Fe8a03c2e40d59ec63338b96ca3d8%2Fnc-tumpak-sewu-s-majestic-waterfall-colas-decloitre.jpg 2600w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x3000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F75%2Fc3%2Fe8a03c2e40d59ec63338b96ca3d8%2Fnc-tumpak-sewu-s-majestic-waterfall-colas-decloitre.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1300px) 1238px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 60px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x3000+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F75%2Fc3%2Fe8a03c2e40d59ec63338b96ca3d8%2Fnc-tumpak-sewu-s-majestic-waterfall-colas-decloitre.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x3000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F75%2Fc3%2Fe8a03c2e40d59ec63338b96ca3d8%2Fnc-tumpak-sewu-s-majestic-waterfall-colas-decloitre.jpg" class="img" alt="The stunning Tumpak Sewu cascades like liquid silver from the cliffs, with the powerful Senaru Volcano rising in the distance, sending smoke into the sky as the landscape unfolds in all its natural glory." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 The Tumpak Sewu waterfall in Indonesia cascades from the cliffs. The drone's eye view shows Senaru Volcano rising in the distance, sending smoke into the sky.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Colas Decloitre                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;In this photo, highly commended in the Nature category, an imposing horseshoe-shaped waterfall spills over the cliffs of East Java, Indonesia, at sunrise&lt;strong&gt;. &lt;/strong&gt;Boston-based, French-British drone photographer&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://colas-drone-photography.com/" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Colas Decloitre&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; had hoped to capture the interesting shape of the waterfall with Mount Semeru rising behind it. What he hadn't anticipated was catching the active volcano behind the waterfall, glowing red and writhed with ash, in the middle of an eruption.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"The only way to get the right alignment of the waterfall and the volcano is with a drone, as you can only be on the side of the waterfall yourself," he says. Using his drone, he could position the waterfall against the volcano, revealing an intriguing landscape that could only be viewed from the air.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Argentine Puna: The Last Ember&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-150689" class="bucketwrap image x-large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 9021;         --source-height: 6595;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9021x6595+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F89%2F87%2F899ecb234e73b09da0f304f05ffd%2Fnc-the-last-ember-isabella-tabacchi.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9021x6595+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F89%2F87%2F899ecb234e73b09da0f304f05ffd%2Fnc-the-last-ember-isabella-tabacchi.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9021x6595+0+0/resize/1000/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F89%2F87%2F899ecb234e73b09da0f304f05ffd%2Fnc-the-last-ember-isabella-tabacchi.jpg 1000w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9021x6595+0+0/resize/1300/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F89%2F87%2F899ecb234e73b09da0f304f05ffd%2Fnc-the-last-ember-isabella-tabacchi.jpg 1300w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9021x6595+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F89%2F87%2F899ecb234e73b09da0f304f05ffd%2Fnc-the-last-ember-isabella-tabacchi.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9021x6595+0+0/resize/2000/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F89%2F87%2F899ecb234e73b09da0f304f05ffd%2Fnc-the-last-ember-isabella-tabacchi.jpg 2000w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9021x6595+0+0/resize/2600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F89%2F87%2F899ecb234e73b09da0f304f05ffd%2Fnc-the-last-ember-isabella-tabacchi.jpg 2600w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9021x6595+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F89%2F87%2F899ecb234e73b09da0f304f05ffd%2Fnc-the-last-ember-isabella-tabacchi.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1300px) 1238px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 60px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9021x6595+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F89%2F87%2F899ecb234e73b09da0f304f05ffd%2Fnc-the-last-ember-isabella-tabacchi.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9021x6595+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F89%2F87%2F899ecb234e73b09da0f304f05ffd%2Fnc-the-last-ember-isabella-tabacchi.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9021x6595+0+0/resize/1000/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F89%2F87%2F899ecb234e73b09da0f304f05ffd%2Fnc-the-last-ember-isabella-tabacchi.jpg 1000w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9021x6595+0+0/resize/1300/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F89%2F87%2F899ecb234e73b09da0f304f05ffd%2Fnc-the-last-ember-isabella-tabacchi.jpg 1300w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9021x6595+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F89%2F87%2F899ecb234e73b09da0f304f05ffd%2Fnc-the-last-ember-isabella-tabacchi.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9021x6595+0+0/resize/2000/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F89%2F87%2F899ecb234e73b09da0f304f05ffd%2Fnc-the-last-ember-isabella-tabacchi.jpg 2000w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9021x6595+0+0/resize/2600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F89%2F87%2F899ecb234e73b09da0f304f05ffd%2Fnc-the-last-ember-isabella-tabacchi.jpg 2600w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9021x6595+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F89%2F87%2F899ecb234e73b09da0f304f05ffd%2Fnc-the-last-ember-isabella-tabacchi.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1300px) 1238px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 60px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9021x6595+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F89%2F87%2F899ecb234e73b09da0f304f05ffd%2Fnc-the-last-ember-isabella-tabacchi.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9021x6595+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F89%2F87%2F899ecb234e73b09da0f304f05ffd%2Fnc-the-last-ember-isabella-tabacchi.jpg" class="img" alt="default" loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 A small scoria cone glows crimson amid the volcanic deserts of the Argentine Puna. Surrounded by ancient lava flows, ash deposits and wind-sculpted terrain, it stands as a final ember in a landscape forged by fire.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Isabella Tabacchi                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;It looks like the glowing eye of a fiery monster.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;It's actually a volcanic cone, the pile of rock, ash and hardened lava that builds up around the mouth of the volcano over time.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The Last Ember&lt;/em&gt;, by Italy-based photographer &lt;a href="https://www.isabellatabacchi.com/" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Isabella Tabacchi&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, is an example of how a drone photo has the power to transform landscapes into a dream-like quality. It was a commended entry in the Nature category.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;The photo was taken in the Argentine Puna, a vast, remote, high-altitude plateau in the Andes of northwestern Argentina: a landscape of volcanoes, ancient lava fields, salt flats and desert mountains. The cone's reddish color comes from iron-bearing minerals in the volcanic rock, while the surrounding dark terrain consists of lava that cooled and hardened long ago.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Exploring these volcanic landscapes requires careful planning, long journeys across remote terrain and constant attention to the conditions. "At high elevations, the thin air and rapidly changing weather can also make drone operations more demanding," Tabacchi says.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Her winning photo was a case of serendipity.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"I captured it during an exploratory flight, while studying the volcanic landscape and experimenting with different compositions," she says. "It wasn't even photographed during the golden hour [shortly after sunrise or before sunset] which is usually the time I prefer for landscape photography."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"When I reviewed my photographs, I found myself much more attracted to this earlier composition. There was something about the geometry of the lava field, the small red cone and the immense volcanic wilderness surrounding it that felt far more powerful to me than the warmer, more traditionally dramatic light of the other photograph."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;It reminded Tabacchi of an important lesson she learned throughout her photographic career: Extraordinary landscapes don't always need extraordinary light to create a compelling image.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"Sometimes the strength of a photograph comes from the subject itself, its shapes, its geological history and the unexpected perspective from which we discover it," she says.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lake Natron: What Lies Beneath&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-150691" class="bucketwrap image x-large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 7394;         --source-height: 5133;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7394x5133+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa3%2Ffb%2F803741c147dba63f83e0697a3078%2Fnc-what-lies-beneath-holly-kirkland.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7394x5133+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa3%2Ffb%2F803741c147dba63f83e0697a3078%2Fnc-what-lies-beneath-holly-kirkland.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7394x5133+0+0/resize/1000/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa3%2Ffb%2F803741c147dba63f83e0697a3078%