cf0%2Fak-flooding-4.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F07%2F29%2Fcf185dbe4a469359a44abcb0ecf0%2Fak-flooding-4.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F07%2F29%2Fcf185dbe4a469359a44abcb0ecf0%2Fak-flooding-4.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F07%2F29%2Fcf185dbe4a469359a44abcb0ecf0%2Fak-flooding-4.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F07%2F29%2Fcf185dbe4a469359a44abcb0ecf0%2Fak-flooding-4.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F07%2F29%2Fcf185dbe4a469359a44abcb0ecf0%2Fak-flooding-4.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F07%2F29%2Fcf185dbe4a469359a44abcb0ecf0%2Fak-flooding-4.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F07%2F29%2Fcf185dbe4a469359a44abcb0ecf0%2Fak-flooding-4.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F07%2F29%2Fcf185dbe4a469359a44abcb0ecf0%2Fak-flooding-4.jpg" class="img" alt="Workers helping clear debris from the tundra around Kipnuk 10 and construction crews work on houses and other building throughout the area 10 months after ex-typhoon Halong hit Alaska&amp;#039;s coast in October of 2025. Construction crews work on houses and other building throughout Kipnuk after ex-typhoon Halong hit Alaska&amp;#039;s coast in October of 2025." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Workers helping clear debris from the tundra around Kipnuk and construction crews working on houses 10 months after ex-typhoon Halong hit Alaska's coast in October of 2025.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Gabby Hiestand Salgado/KYUK                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Challenges remain in moving back&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;This work is critical to getting Kipnuk's homes in shape to live in again, but the town is far from being fully restored.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;aside id="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" class="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" aria-label="recommended stories"&gt;&lt;/aside&gt;    &lt;!-- END ID="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" CLASS="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" ARIA-LABEL="RECOMMENDED STORIES" --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;According to the state, most people in Kipnuk didn't have home or flood insurance. They estimate that funds from the Federal Emergency Management Agency will make most of the homes livable by Thanksgiving – meaning replacing wet insulation and repairing windows, doors and roofs. But the funds won't be enough to return some severely damaged homes to how they were before the storm. &lt;a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1M7QoYnZ9RlZ90iKNre78_Q3XLVDN2Een/view?usp=sharing" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;u&gt;The state is currently appealing &lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;for additional funding to build replacement housing.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resnx-s1-6021471-102" class="bucketwrap internallink insettwocolumn inset2col"&gt;                     &lt;!-- END CLASS="BUCKET IMG" --&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;     &lt;!-- END ID="RESNX-S1-6021471-102" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP INTERNALLINK INSETTWOCOLUMN INSET2COL " --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;There's also no estimate on when the school will reopen.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Leona Paul, who has been working as a cook to feed the construction teams, says even if the houses are habitable, some people were too traumatized by the storm to return.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"I think it's too overwhelming for them," she says, "especially the older people."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resnx-s1-6021471-103" class="bucketwrap internallink insettwocolumn inset2col"&gt;                     &lt;!-- END CLASS="BUCKET IMG" --&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;     &lt;!-- END ID="RESNX-S1-6021471-103" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP INTERNALLINK INSETTWOCOLUMN INSET2COL " --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;And climate change is making towns like Kipnuk &lt;a href="https://www.commerce.alaska.gov/web/dcra/ResiliencePlanningLandManagement/ACCIMP/HazardImpactAssessments/KipnukHIA" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;u&gt;more vulnerable to future storms&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. Most people in town &lt;a href="https://www.kyuk.org/public-safety/2026-03-21/kipnuk-votes-to-relocate-following-devastation-from-halong" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;u&gt;want to rebuild the village&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; somewhere safer but the funding they have received so far from FEMA can only go towards &lt;a href="https://www.fema.gov/node/what-should-fema-home-repair-money-be-used" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;u&gt;restoring what was damaged&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. Kipnuk hasn't yet found the money to move.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-150949" class="bucketwrap image x-large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 1500;         --source-height: 1000;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1500x1000+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F5d%2F84%2Fc2d214c74c56920519e557ca25bf%2F260811-gsalgado-kipnuk-05919.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1500x1000+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F5d%2F84%2Fc2d214c74c56920519e557ca25bf%2F260811-gsalgado-kipnuk-05919.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1500x1000+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F5d%2F84%2Fc2d214c74c56920519e557ca25bf%2F260811-gsalgado-kipnuk-05919.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1500x1000+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F5d%2F84%2Fc2d214c74c56920519e557ca25bf%2F260811-gsalgado-kipnuk-05919.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1500x1000+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F5d%2F84%2Fc2d214c74c56920519e557ca25bf%2F260811-gsalgado-kipnuk-05919.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1500x1000+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F5d%2F84%2Fc2d214c74c56920519e557ca25bf%2F260811-gsalgado-kipnuk-05919.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1500x1000+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F5d%2F84%2Fc2d214c74c56920519e557ca25bf%2F260811-gsalgado-kipnuk-05919.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1500x1000+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F5d%2F84%2Fc2d214c74c56920519e557ca25bf%2F260811-gsalgado-kipnuk-05919.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1500x1000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F5d%2F84%2Fc2d214c74c56920519e557ca25bf%2F260811-gsalgado-kipnuk-05919.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1500x1000+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F5d%2F84%2Fc2d214c74c56920519e557ca25bf%2F260811-gsalgado-kipnuk-05919.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1500x1000+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F5d%2F84%2Fc2d214c74c56920519e557ca25bf%2F260811-gsalgado-kipnuk-05919.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1500x1000+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F5d%2F84%2Fc2d214c74c56920519e557ca25bf%2F260811-gsalgado-kipnuk-05919.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1500x1000+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F5d%2F84%2Fc2d214c74c56920519e557ca25bf%2F260811-gsalgado-kipnuk-05919.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1500x1000+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F5d%2F84%2Fc2d214c74c56920519e557ca25bf%2F260811-gsalgado-kipnuk-05919.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1500x1000+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F5d%2F84%2Fc2d214c74c56920519e557ca25bf%2F260811-gsalgado-kipnuk-05919.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1500x1000+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F5d%2F84%2Fc2d214c74c56920519e557ca25bf%2F260811-gsalgado-kipnuk-05919.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1500x1000+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F5d%2F84%2Fc2d214c74c56920519e557ca25bf%2F260811-gsalgado-kipnuk-05919.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1500x1000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F5d%2F84%2Fc2d214c74c56920519e557ca25bf%2F260811-gsalgado-kipnuk-05919.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1500x1000+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F5d%2F84%2Fc2d214c74c56920519e557ca25bf%2F260811-gsalgado-kipnuk-05919.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1500x1000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F5d%2F84%2Fc2d214c74c56920519e557ca25bf%2F260811-gsalgado-kipnuk-05919.jpg" class="img" alt="Kipnuk ten months after ex-typhoon Halong hit Alaska&amp;#039;s coast in October of 2025." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 In August, damage from the October 2025 storm was still visible in Kipnuk.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Gabby Hiestand Salgado/KYUK                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Living away from home takes a toll&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Right now residents may not have a better option other than moving back. Many say living in bigger towns, or cities like Anchorage, has been tough. People aren't speaking as much Yugtun – the native language. They're farther from loved ones. Their kids, who are used to playing all over town, have to watch out for cars.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Leona Paul, who spent part of the summer in Kipnuk, says she likes being there&lt;strong&gt;. &lt;/strong&gt;"You're free to do anything you want," she says. "In a city you just can't do whatever you want."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Being displaced from the village has also meant separation from the Alaska Native cultural practices of hunting and gathering traditional food on the land.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resnx-s1-6021471-104" class="bucketwrap internallink insettwocolumn inset2col"&gt;                     &lt;!-- END CLASS="BUCKET IMG" --&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;     &lt;!-- END ID="RESNX-S1-6021471-104" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP INTERNALLINK INSETTWOCOLUMN INSET2COL " --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Some residents, like Burt Paul's family, traveled home for the summer to practice subsistence and be together.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Upriver from Kipnuk on a lush tundra bluff, his family filled buckets with sweet, orange salmonberries, or &lt;em&gt;naunraqs&lt;/em&gt; as they are called in coastal Yugtun. He says after last fall's destruction – he didn't know when he'd see these native plants growing again.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"It beats my mind that I see food growing, grass growing, fish coming in," he says.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-150947" class="bucketwrap image x-large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 5366;         --source-height: 3578;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5366x3578+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F39%2F4f%2Fdc4c34d64ca2b0065e39e834384f%2Fimg-0824-2.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5366x3578+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F39%2F4f%2Fdc4c34d64ca2b0065e39e834384f%2Fimg-0824-2.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5366x3578+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F39%2F4f%2Fdc4c34d64ca2b0065e39e834384f%2Fimg-0824-2.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5366x3578+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F39%2F4f%2Fdc4c34d64ca2b0065e39e834384f%2Fimg-0824-2.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5366x3578+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F39%2F4f%2Fdc4c34d64ca2b0065e39e834384f%2Fimg-0824-2.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5366x3578+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F39%2F4f%2Fdc4c34d64ca2b0065e39e834384f%2Fimg-0824-2.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5366x3578+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F39%2F4f%2Fdc4c34d64ca2b0065e39e834384f%2Fimg-0824-2.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5366x3578+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F39%2F4f%2Fdc4c34d64ca2b0065e39e834384f%2Fimg-0824-2.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5366x3578+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F39%2F4f%2Fdc4c34d64ca2b0065e39e834384f%2Fimg-0824-2.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5366x3578+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F39%2F4f%2Fdc4c34d64ca2b0065e39e834384f%2Fimg-0824-2.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5366x3578+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F39%2F4f%2Fdc4c34d64ca2b0065e39e834384f%2Fimg-0824-2.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5366x3578+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F39%2F4f%2Fdc4c34d64ca2b0065e39e834384f%2Fimg-0824-2.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5366x3578+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F39%2F4f%2Fdc4c34d64ca2b0065e39e834384f%2Fimg-0824-2.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5366x3578+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F39%2F4f%2Fdc4c34d64ca2b0065e39e834384f%2Fimg-0824-2.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5366x3578+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F39%2F4f%2Fdc4c34d64ca2b0065e39e834384f%2Fimg-0824-2.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5366x3578+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F39%2F4f%2Fdc4c34d64ca2b0065e39e834384f%2Fimg-0824-2.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5366x3578+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F39%2F4f%2Fdc4c34d64ca2b0065e39e834384f%2Fimg-0824-2.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5366x3578+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F39%2F4f%2Fdc4c34d64ca2b0065e39e834384f%2Fimg-0824-2.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5366x3578+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F39%2F4f%2Fdc4c34d64ca2b0065e39e834384f%2Fimg-0824-2.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5366x3578+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F39%2F4f%2Fdc4c34d64ca2b0065e39e834384f%2Fimg-0824-2.jpg" class="img" alt="Burt Paul’s family, traveled home for the summer to practice subsistence and be together on August 12, 2026. Upriver from Kipnuk on a lush tundra bluff, they filled buckets with sweet, orange salmonberries, or naunraqs as they are called in coastal Yugtun." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Burt Paul's family traveled home for the summer to practice subsistence and be together. On August 12, 2026, they went berry-picking upriver from Kipnuk.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Samantha Watson/KYUK                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Paul's family evacuated after the storm, but he stayed behind in Kipnuk, acting as a community leader through the aftermath. Usually, his family goes camping and berry picking for days. This summer, their trips were shorter – confined to when everyone was in town.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;Short as those trips may have been, he says they were important: &lt;em&gt;"&lt;/em&gt;We have to keep things going some way, somehow, no matter what situation we go through," he says.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;He's not sure when his family – or his village – will all be back together again.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
