.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ffb%2F84%2F866bc8f646f18463e046f53cc35c%2Fwvdatacenter-15.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ffb%2F84%2F866bc8f646f18463e046f53cc35c%2Fwvdatacenter-15.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ffb%2F84%2F866bc8f646f18463e046f53cc35c%2Fwvdatacenter-15.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ffb%2F84%2F866bc8f646f18463e046f53cc35c%2Fwvdatacenter-15.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ffb%2F84%2F866bc8f646f18463e046f53cc35c%2Fwvdatacenter-15.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ffb%2F84%2F866bc8f646f18463e046f53cc35c%2Fwvdatacenter-15.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ffb%2F84%2F866bc8f646f18463e046f53cc35c%2Fwvdatacenter-15.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ffb%2F84%2F866bc8f646f18463e046f53cc35c%2Fwvdatacenter-15.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ffb%2F84%2F866bc8f646f18463e046f53cc35c%2Fwvdatacenter-15.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ffb%2F84%2F866bc8f646f18463e046f53cc35c%2Fwvdatacenter-15.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ffb%2F84%2F866bc8f646f18463e046f53cc35c%2Fwvdatacenter-15.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ffb%2F84%2F866bc8f646f18463e046f53cc35c%2Fwvdatacenter-15.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ffb%2F84%2F866bc8f646f18463e046f53cc35c%2Fwvdatacenter-15.jpg" class="img" alt="White Grass Ski Touring Center in Canaan Valley , W.Va., is celebrated for its unusually curvy and hilly cross-country skiing terrain." fetchpriority="high" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 White Grass Ski Touring Center in Canaan Valley , W.Va., is celebrated for its unusually curvy and hilly cross-country skiing terrain.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Chris Jackson for NPR                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;DAVIS, W.Va. — Stretching nearly a million acres through the rugged mountains of eastern West Virginia, the Monongahela National Forest links some of the state's best known natural attractions. The vast area ranges from the ski slopes of Canaan Valley to the dark skies of Blackwater Falls and Spruce Knob and includes the small towns of Davis and Thomas that serve as gateways for visitors to the region.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resnx-s1-5992790-100" class="bucketwrap internallink insettwocolumn inset2col"&gt;                     &lt;!-- END CLASS="BUCKET IMG" --&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;     &lt;!-- END ID="RESNX-S1-5992790-100" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP INTERNALLINK INSETTWOCOLUMN INSET2COL " --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;For the past seven months, Kaleb Skelton, his wife, Ella, their 2-year-old son, Ryder, and dog Mabel have lived in a camper in this corner of West Virginia's "almost heaven." Kaleb is finishing a seasonal stint as a campground manager on a lake near Spruce Knob, the state's highest point.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;On clear nights atop the isolated peak, they get to experience a river of stars in one of the &lt;a href="https://lightpollutionmap.app/?lat=38.699836&amp;lng=-79.532828&amp;zoom=6" target="_blank"&gt;very few pockets of darkness&lt;/a&gt; remaining in the Eastern United States. The area has become a draw for amateur astronomers.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;div id="resg-s1-150628" class="bucketwrap image medium"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 3000;         --source-height: 4500;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbb%2F72%2F57cb78714864aec98369e672d87a%2Fwvdatacenter-4.jpg 200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/300/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbb%2F72%2F57cb78714864aec98369e672d87a%2Fwvdatacenter-4.jpg 300w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbb%2F72%2F57cb78714864aec98369e672d87a%2Fwvdatacenter-4.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbb%2F72%2F57cb78714864aec98369e672d87a%2Fwvdatacenter-4.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbb%2F72%2F57cb78714864aec98369e672d87a%2Fwvdatacenter-4.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbb%2F72%2F57cb78714864aec98369e672d87a%2Fwvdatacenter-4.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbb%2F72%2F57cb78714864aec98369e672d87a%2Fwvdatacenter-4.jpg 1600w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbb%2F72%2F57cb78714864aec98369e672d87a%2Fwvdatacenter-4.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 298px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(((100vw - 365px)/3) - 30px), (min-width: 768px) calc(((100vw - 30px)/3) - 30px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbb%2F72%2F57cb78714864aec98369e672d87a%2Fwvdatacenter-4.jpg 200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/300/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbb%2F72%2F57cb78714864aec98369e672d87a%2Fwvdatacenter-4.jpg 300w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbb%2F72%2F57cb78714864aec98369e672d87a%2Fwvdatacenter-4.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbb%2F72%2F57cb78714864aec98369e672d87a%2Fwvdatacenter-4.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbb%2F72%2F57cb78714864aec98369e672d87a%2Fwvdatacenter-4.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbb%2F72%2F57cb78714864aec98369e672d87a%2Fwvdatacenter-4.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbb%2F72%2F57cb78714864aec98369e672d87a%2Fwvdatacenter-4.jpg 1600w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbb%2F72%2F57cb78714864aec98369e672d87a%2Fwvdatacenter-4.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 298px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(((100vw - 365px)/3) - 30px), (min-width: 768px) calc(((100vw - 30px)/3) - 30px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbb%2F72%2F57cb78714864aec98369e672d87a%2Fwvdatacenter-4.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbb%2F72%2F57cb78714864aec98369e672d87a%2Fwvdatacenter-4.jpg" class="img" alt="Spruce Knob Lake Campground hosts Kaleb and Ella Skelton, at their site in West Virginia on  Oct. 10. The couple from Texas have been at Spruce Knob since April and said they have never seen darker skies than atop West Virginia&amp;#039;s highest point." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Spruce Knob Lake Campground hosts Kaleb and Ella Skelton, at their site at Spruce Knob on Saturday, Oct. 10 2026 in Spruce Knob, W.Va.  The couple from Texas have been at the site since April and said they have never seen darker skies than atop Spruce Knob.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Chris Jackson for NPR                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;During summer's new moons, Kaleb says, one in four campsites he oversees is occupied by someone with a telescope. He thought his family's cabin in eastern Texas offered "the craziest" dark skies he'd ever seen, "but coming out here definitely rivals it."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;A dark history for 'Stump Town'&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Those inky-black nights — and the natural beauty they shelter — are now under threat from what many residents see as a modern-day version of extractive industries like logging and mining that once defined the region. In a place where tourism, outdoor recreation and community are deeply intertwined, a gigantic power plant and data center campus in nearby Tucker County would bring large-scale development into the heart of it all.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;A stark image of the town of Davis from 1885, during the heyday of logging, is a reminder of that transformation. The photo shows a handful of squat buildings amid a broad clearing littered with forest remains.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;They used to call it "Stump Town," says Kim Williams, president of the Snow Sports Museum of West Virginia in Canaan Valley. At the turn of the century, massive first-growth trees dominated the landscape.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Then, logging companies "came in and clear-cut the whole valley and everything around it," he says.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resnx-s1-5992790-101" class="bucketwrap internallink insettwocolumn inset2col"&gt;                     &lt;!-- END CLASS="BUCKET IMG" --&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;     &lt;!-- END ID="RESNX-S1-5992790-101" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP INTERNALLINK INSETTWOCOLUMN INSET2COL " --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;By the early 20th century, entire mountainsides of red spruce and eastern hemlock had been stripped bare. Then came the coal companies, which left the nearby Blackwater River acidic and dangerous to drink.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Today, the scars still show. The big trees won't return for generations, but a century of natural regrowth, conservation and deliberate restoration&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;means the land is on its way to healing.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;While few expect that the latest tech boom presages anything like the environmental destruction of the past, many see the proposed new Ridgeline data center as a big step backward, undoing the progress the local community has made to recover.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;A roughly 785-megawatt generating plant is slated to be the first part of "a large-scale data and energy infrastructure project designed to support artificial intelligence, cloud computing, and enterprise systems," according to &lt;a href="https://fundamentaldata.com/" target="_blank"&gt;Purcellville, Va.-based Fundamental Data LLC&lt;/a&gt;, the company behind Ridgeline.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-150629" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 5485;         --source-height: 3577;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5485x3577+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F7c%2F15%2F1b2d621b41929538d7f98175433c%2Fmaster-pnp-det-4a00000-4a09000-4a09300-4a09388u.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5485x3577+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F7c%2F15%2F1b2d621b41929538d7f98175433c%2Fmaster-pnp-det-4a00000-4a09000-4a09300-4a09388u.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5485x3577+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F7c%2F15%2F1b2d621b41929538d7f98175433c%2Fmaster-pnp-det-4a00000-4a09000-4a09300-4a09388u.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5485x3577+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F7c%2F15%2F1b2d621b41929538d7f98175433c%2Fmaster-pnp-det-4a00000-4a09000-4a09300-4a09388u.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5485x3577+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F7c%2F15%2F1b2d621b41929538d7f98175433c%2Fmaster-pnp-det-4a00000-4a09000-4a09300-4a09388u.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5485x3577+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F7c%2F15%2F1b2d621b41929538d7f98175433c%2Fmaster-pnp-det-4a00000-4a09000-4a09300-4a09388u.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5485x3577+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F7c%2F15%2F1b2d621b41929538d7f98175433c%2Fmaster-pnp-det-4a00000-4a09000-4a09300-4a09388u.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5485x3577+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F7c%2F15%2F1b2d621b41929538d7f98175433c%2Fmaster-pnp-det-4a00000-4a09000-4a09300-4a09388u.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5485x3577+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F7c%2F15%2F1b2d621b41929538d7f98175433c%2Fmaster-pnp-det-4a00000-4a09000-4a09300-4a09388u.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5485x3577+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F7c%2F15%2F1b2d621b41929538d7f98175433c%2Fmaster-pnp-det-4a00000-4a09000-4a09300-4a09388u.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5485x3577+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F7c%2F15%2F1b2d621b41929538d7f98175433c%2Fmaster-pnp-det-4a00000-4a09000-4a09300-4a09388u.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5485x3577+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F7c%2F15%2F1b2d621b41929538d7f98175433c%2Fmaster-pnp-det-4a00000-4a09000-4a09300-4a09388u.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5485x3577+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F7c%2F15%2F1b2d621b41929538d7f98175433c%2Fmaster-pnp-det-4a00000-4a09000-4a09300-4a09388u.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5485x3577+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F7c%2F15%2F1b2d621b41929538d7f98175433c%2Fmaster-pnp-det-4a00000-4a09000-4a09300-4a09388u.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5485x3577+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F7c%2F15%2F1b2d621b41929538d7f98175433c%2Fmaster-pnp-det-4a00000-4a09000-4a09300-4a09388u.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5485x3577+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F7c%2F15%2F1b2d621b41929538d7f98175433c%2Fmaster-pnp-det-4a00000-4a09000-4a09300-4a09388u.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5485x3577+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F7c%2F15%2F1b2d621b41929538d7f98175433c%2Fmaster-pnp-det-4a00000-4a09000-4a09300-4a09388u.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5485x3577+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F7c%2F15%2F1b2d621b41929538d7f98175433c%2Fmaster-pnp-det-4a00000-4a09000-4a09300-4a09388u.jpg" class="img" alt="The photo &amp;quot;The Birth of a city, Davis, W. Va. in 1885&amp;quot; by William Henry Jackson" loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 The photo "The Birth of a city, Davis, W. Va. in 1885" by William Henry Jackson shows a handful of squat buildings amid a broad clearing littered with forest remains.                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;  &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;The complex would rely primarily on natural gas, with diesel as a backup fuel source. Power generated on-site, rather than purchased from the regional grid, could ease some concerns about the project's effects on electricity rates. It does not, however, resolve concerns over air and water pollution.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;aside id="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" class="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" aria-label="recommended stories"&gt;&lt;/aside&gt;    &lt;!-- END ID="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" CLASS="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" ARIA-LABEL="RECOMMENDED STORIES" --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Located on a reclaimed coal-mining site, plans are for an initial 291 acres that &lt;a href="https://blueridgeleader.com/from-purcellville-to-west-virginia/" target="_blank"&gt;could eventually expand to 10,000 acres&lt;/a&gt; — 15 square miles — and &lt;a href="https://www.wvgazettemail.com/news/energy_and_environment/wv-axes-fundamental-data-violation-notice-saying-large-scale-project-conceptual/article_5353b642-4a8e-4a4e-a048-ddc0c3afcf6c.html" target="_blank"&gt;include parts of neighboring Grant County&lt;/a&gt;, according to local news reports.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Speaking to NPR, Casey Chapman, listed in court documents as Fundamental Data's "responsible individual," declined to speculate on the facility's ultimate size, saying only that "if fully developed … it would be thousands of acres."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resnx-s1-5992790-102" class="bucketwrap internallink insettwocolumn inset2col"&gt;                     &lt;!-- END CLASS="BUCKET IMG" --&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;     &lt;!-- END ID="RESNX-S1-5992790-102" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP INTERNALLINK INSETTWOCOLUMN INSET2COL " --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Light pollution is a &lt;a href="https://www.nbcwashington.com/news/local/northern-virginia/data-center-light-noise-pollution-reston-residents/4165305/" target="_blank"&gt;common complaint&lt;/a&gt; from residents living near data centers. Chapman says the company will use "well-designed" lighting to help minimize the effects of sky glow, in an effort not to jeopardize nearby Blackwater Falls State Park's pursuit of &lt;a href="https://darksky.org/what-we-do/international-dark-sky-places/" target="_blank"&gt;an official dark-sky certification&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;An &lt;a href="https://darksky.astrowl.com/tucker-county-dark-skies.html" target="_blank"&gt;analysis&lt;/a&gt; by the Northern Virginia Astronomy Club, which hosts an annual star party in the region, found that Ridgeline's initial footprint could increase sky glow near Blackwater by 528%, transforming its nighttime rural sky to one comparable to a suburban area. (The same analysis found only a minimal impact on Spruce Knob.)&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;But safety and security — not light pollution — take precedence, Chapman says. The facility will be "an industrial plant that runs around the clock," he notes. "Crews need proper lighting to operate and maintain equipment safely."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Opponents face an uphill battle&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Chip Chase is among the skeptics. He runs White Grass Ski Touring Center, a popular cross-country ski area that he helped found 45 years ago. He is a fixture in the local community that he describes as "Vermont, with Southern hospitality."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"If you're an outdoor person, this place is paradise," he says. "People come here to get away from data centers. People want dark skies here. People want to have a peaceful, quiet recreational area."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-150631" class="bucketwrap image x-large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 4500;         --source-height: 3000;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F3c%2Fedfbfe884300b60b7e82621313cf%2Fwvdatacenter-40.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F3c%2Fedfbfe884300b60b7e82621313cf%2Fwvdatacenter-40.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F3c%2Fedfbfe884300b60b7e82621313cf%2Fwvdatacenter-40.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F3c%2Fedfbfe884300b60b7e82621313cf%2Fwvdatacenter-40.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F3c%2Fedfbfe884300b60b7e82621313cf%2Fwvdatacenter-40.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F3c%2Fedfbfe884300b60b7e82621313cf%2Fwvdatacenter-40.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F3c%2Fedfbfe884300b60b7e82621313cf%2Fwvdatacenter-40.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F3c%2Fedfbfe884300b60b7e82621313cf%2Fwvdatacenter-40.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F3c%2Fedfbfe884300b60b7e82621313cf%2Fwvdatacenter-40.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F3c%2Fedfbfe884300b60b7e82621313cf%2Fwvdatacenter-40.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F3c%2Fedfbfe884300b60b7e82621313cf%2Fwvdatacenter-40.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F3c%2Fedfbfe884300b60b7e82621313cf%2Fwvdatacenter-40.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F3c%2Fedfbfe884300b60b7e82621313cf%2Fwvdatacenter-40.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F3c%2Fedfbfe884300b60b7e82621313cf%2Fwvdatacenter-40.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F3c%2Fedfbfe884300b60b7e82621313cf%2Fwvdatacenter-40.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F3c%2Fedfbfe884300b60b7e82621313cf%2Fwvdatacenter-40.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F3c%2Fedfbfe884300b60b7e82621313cf%2Fwvdatacenter-40.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F3c%2Fedfbfe884300b60b7e82621313cf%2Fwvdatacenter-40.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F3c%2Fedfbfe884300b60b7e82621313cf%2Fwvdatacenter-40.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F3c%2Fedfbfe884300b60b7e82621313cf%2Fwvdatacenter-40.jpg" class="img" alt="Chip Chase, co-founder of Whitegrass Touring Center, at the cross-country ski resort on Sunday October 11, 2026 in Canaan Valley, W.Va." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Chip Chase, co-founder of White Grass Ski Touring Center, at the cross-country ski resort in Canaan Valley, W.Va., on Oct. 11.&lt;br&gt;                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Chris Jackson for NPR                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Economic development, however, is a top priority for the state of West Virginia. It ranks among the poorest in the country and has the &lt;a href="https://factsmaps.com/us-states-population-growth-rate-1950-2016/" target="_blank"&gt;unique distinction of having lost population since 1950&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;John Deskins, director of the West Virginia University Bureau of Business and Economic Research, says data centers could be a boon. "As long as we're making sure that we follow all the proper procedures around noise pollution, water pollution, [and] other elements of environmental pollution ... I think they're a good opportunity," he says.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resnx-s1-5992790-103" class="bucketwrap internallink insettwocolumn inset2col"&gt;                     &lt;!-- END CLASS="BUCKET IMG" --&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;     &lt;!-- END ID="RESNX-S1-5992790-103" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP INTERNALLINK INSETTWOCOLUMN INSET2COL " --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;It is those proper procedures that worry people in Tucker United, a grassroots group opposing the data center plans. As in so many other places across the country, they are battling what they see as a lack of transparency.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;The first anyone in the community heard about the Ridgeline project was March 2025, when an obscure notice appeared in a local newspaper announcing the request for an air-quality permit for a proposed power plant, says Davis Mayor Alan Tomson. A resident called him to ask if he knew anything about it. "I told her that I did not," Tomson says. He then called the mayor of neighboring Thomas. "He also had not heard anything about it."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-150634" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 3000;         --source-height: 4500;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F77%2Fbe%2F6365c3b54df58c421c3b7e168b60%2Fwvdatacenter-41.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F77%2Fbe%2F6365c3b54df58c421c3b7e168b60%2Fwvdatacenter-41.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F77%2Fbe%2F6365c3b54df58c421c3b7e168b60%2Fwvdatacenter-41.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F77%2Fbe%2F6365c3b54df58c421c3b7e168b60%2Fwvdatacenter-41.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F77%2Fbe%2F6365c3b54df58c421c3b7e168b60%2Fwvdatacenter-41.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F77%2Fbe%2F6365c3b54df58c421c3b7e168b60%2Fwvdatacenter-41.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F77%2Fbe%2F6365c3b54df58c421c3b7e168b60%2Fwvdatacenter-41.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F77%2Fbe%2F6365c3b54df58c421c3b7e168b60%2Fwvdatacenter-41.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F77%2Fbe%2F6365c3b54df58c421c3b7e168b60%2Fwvdatacenter-41.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F77%2Fbe%2F6365c3b54df58c421c3b7e168b60%2Fwvdatacenter-41.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F77%2Fbe%2F6365c3b54df58c421c3b7e168b60%2Fwvdatacenter-41.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F77%2Fbe%2F6365c3b54df58c421c3b7e168b60%2Fwvdatacenter-41.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F77%2Fbe%2F6365c3b54df58c421c3b7e168b60%2Fwvdatacenter-41.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F77%2Fbe%2F6365c3b54df58c421c3b7e168b60%2Fwvdatacenter-41.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F77%2Fbe%2F6365c3b54df58c421c3b7e168b60%2Fwvdatacenter-41.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F77%2Fbe%2F6365c3b54df58c421c3b7e168b60%2Fwvdatacenter-41.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F77%2Fbe%2F6365c3b54df58c421c3b7e168b60%2Fwvdatacenter-41.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F77%2Fbe%2F6365c3b54df58c421c3b7e168b60%2Fwvdatacenter-41.jpg" class="img" alt="Davis, W.Va., Mayor Alan Tomson on William Ave." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Mayor Alan Tomson on William Avenue in Davis, W.Va., on Oct. 11.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Chris Jackson for NPR                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;From there, Tomson says, things moved quickly. A month later, the Republican super-majority in both houses of the state legislature passed a highly unusual bill &lt;a href="https://www.wvlegislature.gov/bill_status/bills_text.cfm?billdoc=hb2014+sub1+enr.htm&amp;billtype=B&amp;houseorig=H&amp;i=2014&amp;sesstype=RS&amp;yr=2025" target="_blank"&gt;exempting certified microgrid districts&lt;/a&gt; and high-impact data centers from county or municipal zoning or any local restrictions related to horticultural, noise, viewshed, lighting, development or land use.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;A lack of guardrails&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Opponents quickly gathered 1,000 signatures on a &lt;a href="https://www.change.org/p/protect-local-freedom-urge-governor-morrisey-to-veto-data-center-bill" target="_blank"&gt;petition&lt;/a&gt; urging Republican Gov. Patrick Morrisey to veto the bill. They were unsuccessful. Signing the legislation, &lt;a href="https://governor.wv.gov/article/governor-patrick-morrisey-signs-power-generation-and-consumption-and-one-stop-shop" target="_blank"&gt;the governor noted&lt;/a&gt; the state's need to "continue to focus on economic development and utilizing our many natural resources," adding that "companies will now be able to quickly build, expand, and increase job creation right here in West Virginia." &lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"They completely got rid of any … sort of regulation or guardrails for these data center developments," says Tucker United spokesperson Nikki Forrester. "They want to sell us out, … extract our resources and leave us with the mess."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-150632" class="bucketwrap image x-large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 4500;         --source-height: 3000;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fad%2F70%2Ff2b3f1a945ed8bf54ea6e9d5818d%2Fwvdatacenter-26.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fad%2F70%2Ff2b3f1a945ed8bf54ea6e9d5818d%2Fwvdatacenter-26.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fad%2F70%2Ff2b3f1a945ed8bf54ea6e9d5818d%2Fwvdatacenter-26.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fad%2F70%2Ff2b3f1a945ed8bf54ea6e9d5818d%2Fwvdatacenter-26.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fad%2F70%2Ff2b3f1a945