%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fad%2F70%2Ff2b3f1a945ed8bf54ea6e9d5818d%2Fwvdatacenter-26.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fad%2F70%2Ff2b3f1a945ed8bf54ea6e9d5818d%2Fwvdatacenter-26.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fad%2F70%2Ff2b3f1a945ed8bf54ea6e9d5818d%2Fwvdatacenter-26.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fad%2F70%2Ff2b3f1a945ed8bf54ea6e9d5818d%2Fwvdatacenter-26.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fad%2F70%2Ff2b3f1a945ed8bf54ea6e9d5818d%2Fwvdatacenter-26.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fad%2F70%2Ff2b3f1a945ed8bf54ea6e9d5818d%2Fwvdatacenter-26.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fad%2F70%2Ff2b3f1a945ed8bf54ea6e9d5818d%2Fwvdatacenter-26.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fad%2F70%2Ff2b3f1a945ed8bf54ea6e9d5818d%2Fwvdatacenter-26.jpg" class="img" alt="Pedestrians walk past data center protest signs on Front Street in Thomas, W.Va." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Pedestrians walk past data center protest signs on Front Street in Thomas, W.Va.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Chris Jackson for NPR                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;The West Virginia Department of Environmental Protection &lt;a href="https://wvpublic.org/story/energy-environment/regulators-reaffirm-approval-for-microgrid-generator-data-center-in-tucker-county/" target="_blank"&gt;approved Fundamental Data's air-quality permit&lt;/a&gt; without, &lt;a href="https://www.wvhighlands.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Notice-of-Appeal-Ridgeline-Final.pdf" target="_blank"&gt;according to Tucker United&lt;/a&gt; and other activist groups, conducting a comprehensive assessment of the facility's potential public-health impacts on the surrounding valley. When asked by NPR about Tucker United's concerns, the West Virginia Department of Environmental Protection responded that it "does not comment on active litigation" and declined an interview request.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;div id="resnx-s1-5992790-104" class="bucketwrap internallink insettwocolumn inset2col"&gt;                     &lt;!-- END CLASS="BUCKET IMG" --&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;     &lt;!-- END ID="RESNX-S1-5992790-104" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP INTERNALLINK INSETTWOCOLUMN INSET2COL " --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Opponents of the project subsequently commissioned their own &lt;a href="https://www.tuckerunited.com/study" target="_blank"&gt;analysis&lt;/a&gt; finding that the Ridgeline plant could cause between $19 million and $35 million a year in health-related damages and premature deaths.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Tucker United, the West Virginia Highlands Conservancy and the Sierra Club &lt;a href="https://westvirginiawatch.com/2025/12/04/wv-dep-wraps-up-hearing-over-appeal-of-air-quality-permit-for-proposed-tucker-county-power-plant/" target="_blank"&gt;challenged the air-permit decision&lt;/a&gt; in court. Their appeal was dismissed in August on jurisdictional grounds. The groups say they will &lt;a href="https://wvpublic.org/story/energy-environment/community-conservation-groups-ask-courts-to-properly-review-challenges-to-data-center-permitting/amp/" target="_blank"&gt;go to the state's Supreme Court&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Chapman says Tucker United's air-quality study assumes Ridgeline will emit the maximum amount of pollution allowed by its air permit for an entire year, when in fact the permit sets an upper limit and "we're going to operate within those limits," he says.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;There are other environmental concerns.&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;Forrester notes that Canaan Valley's bowl shape and temperature inversions can trap air pollutants near the ground. As for water, she says, "storing 30 million gallons of diesel right on a creek that feeds into our water supplies is really dangerous and puts not just our community, but every community downstream at risk."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-150633" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 3000;         --source-height: 4500;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb0%2Ff5%2F5abf49bb4e3c996ec5bec08bff4e%2Fwvdatacenter-30.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb0%2Ff5%2F5abf49bb4e3c996ec5bec08bff4e%2Fwvdatacenter-30.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb0%2Ff5%2F5abf49bb4e3c996ec5bec08bff4e%2Fwvdatacenter-30.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb0%2Ff5%2F5abf49bb4e3c996ec5bec08bff4e%2Fwvdatacenter-30.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb0%2Ff5%2F5abf49bb4e3c996ec5bec08bff4e%2Fwvdatacenter-30.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb0%2Ff5%2F5abf49bb4e3c996ec5bec08bff4e%2Fwvdatacenter-30.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb0%2Ff5%2F5abf49bb4e3c996ec5bec08bff4e%2Fwvdatacenter-30.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb0%2Ff5%2F5abf49bb4e3c996ec5bec08bff4e%2Fwvdatacenter-30.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb0%2Ff5%2F5abf49bb4e3c996ec5bec08bff4e%2Fwvdatacenter-30.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb0%2Ff5%2F5abf49bb4e3c996ec5bec08bff4e%2Fwvdatacenter-30.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb0%2Ff5%2F5abf49bb4e3c996ec5bec08bff4e%2Fwvdatacenter-30.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb0%2Ff5%2F5abf49bb4e3c996ec5bec08bff4e%2Fwvdatacenter-30.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb0%2Ff5%2F5abf49bb4e3c996ec5bec08bff4e%2Fwvdatacenter-30.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb0%2Ff5%2F5abf49bb4e3c996ec5bec08bff4e%2Fwvdatacenter-30.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb0%2Ff5%2F5abf49bb4e3c996ec5bec08bff4e%2Fwvdatacenter-30.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb0%2Ff5%2F5abf49bb4e3c996ec5bec08bff4e%2Fwvdatacenter-30.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb0%2Ff5%2F5abf49bb4e3c996ec5bec08bff4e%2Fwvdatacenter-30.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x4500+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb0%2Ff5%2F5abf49bb4e3c996ec5bec08bff4e%2Fwvdatacenter-30.jpg" class="img" alt="Nikki Forrester, Director of Communications with Tucker United, in Davis, W.Va on Monday, October 12, 2026." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Nikki Forrester, director of communications with anti-data center group Tucker United, in Davis, W.Va., on Oct. 12.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Chris Jackson for NPR                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Fundamental Data's Chapman says the storage would be safe and that all of the tanks would not need to be filled at any given time.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;In addition to the potential environmental and health hazards, many residents find it particularly galling that&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;West Virginia House Speaker Roger Hanshaw, a Charleston-based attorney with the law firm Bowles Rice, is &lt;a href="https://www.legalnewsline.com/west-virginia-record/hanshaw-representing-data-center-company-in-ica-case/article_4cee2215-7f35-4fea-b590-927a8ea4a021.html" target="_blank"&gt;listed as lead attorney for Fundamental Data&lt;/a&gt; in the permit dispute.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"Here's a guy who's writing laws [and] sponsoring legislation while under contract for one of the people that he's working for," complains Gary Berti, a retired homeowner in Davis. "To me, that's a conflict of interest."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;In an email to NPR, Hanshaw stated: "I am not now, nor have I ever been, employed by Fundamental Data. I am a partner in a law firm. It is public record that the law firm of Bowles Rice is currently counsel for Fundamental Data in a litigation matter pending in West Virginia."&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Jobs are needed, but at what cost? &lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Fundamental Data believes building the Ridgeline facility would bring thousands of temporary jobs and about 500 permanent ones in IT, electrical and cooling systems, engineering and security.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;While no two data center campuses are alike, a &lt;a href="https://www.brookings.edu/articles/new-evidence-on-data-center-employment-effects/" target="_blank"&gt;Brookings Institution study&lt;/a&gt; found that on average, data centers produce around 100 to 200 permanent jobs.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Berti agrees that West Virginia needs jobs, but "there are places that need it more than others," he says, and is skeptical that data centers would bring many permanent workers to the area.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resnx-s1-5992790-105" class="bucketwrap internallink insettwocolumn inset2col"&gt;                     &lt;!-- END CLASS="BUCKET IMG" --&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;     &lt;!-- END ID="RESNX-S1-5992790-105" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP INTERNALLINK INSETTWOCOLUMN INSET2COL " --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;And if artificial intelligence ends up being more hype than substance, he says, it could be a repeat of history.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"A lot of times they leave us behind," he says, referring to the coal and logging industries. "When I moved here 40 years ago, it was two rundown towns," he says, referring to Davis and Thomas. "Look at them now. They're doing well."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-150635" class="bucketwrap image x-large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 4500;         --source-height: 2812;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2812+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2F11%2Fc4f6bc954a6a9d681b180dad72f8%2Fwvdatacenter-45.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2812+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2F11%2Fc4f6bc954a6a9d681b180dad72f8%2Fwvdatacenter-45.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2812+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2F11%2Fc4f6bc954a6a9d681b180dad72f8%2Fwvdatacenter-45.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2812+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2F11%2Fc4f6bc954a6a9d681b180dad72f8%2Fwvdatacenter-45.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2812+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2F11%2Fc4f6bc954a6a9d681b180dad72f8%2Fwvdatacenter-45.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2812+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2F11%2Fc4f6bc954a6a9d681b180dad72f8%2Fwvdatacenter-45.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2812+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2F11%2Fc4f6bc954a6a9d681b180dad72f8%2Fwvdatacenter-45.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2812+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2F11%2Fc4f6bc954a6a9d681b180dad72f8%2Fwvdatacenter-45.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2812+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2F11%2Fc4f6bc954a6a9d681b180dad72f8%2Fwvdatacenter-45.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2812+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2F11%2Fc4f6bc954a6a9d681b180dad72f8%2Fwvdatacenter-45.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2812+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2F11%2Fc4f6bc954a6a9d681b180dad72f8%2Fwvdatacenter-45.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2812+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2F11%2Fc4f6bc954a6a9d681b180dad72f8%2Fwvdatacenter-45.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2812+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2F11%2Fc4f6bc954a6a9d681b180dad72f8%2Fwvdatacenter-45.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2812+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2F11%2Fc4f6bc954a6a9d681b180dad72f8%2Fwvdatacenter-45.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2812+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2F11%2Fc4f6bc954a6a9d681b180dad72f8%2Fwvdatacenter-45.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2812+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2F11%2Fc4f6bc954a6a9d681b180dad72f8%2Fwvdatacenter-45.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2812+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2F11%2Fc4f6bc954a6a9d681b180dad72f8%2Fwvdatacenter-45.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2812+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2F11%2Fc4f6bc954a6a9d681b180dad72f8%2Fwvdatacenter-45.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2812+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2F11%2Fc4f6bc954a6a9d681b180dad72f8%2Fwvdatacenter-45.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2812+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F62%2F11%2Fc4f6bc954a6a9d681b180dad72f8%2Fwvdatacenter-45.jpg" class="img" alt="Davis, W.Va., has a population of roughly" loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Davis, W.Va., has a population of roughly 600 people and attracts tourists from across the country.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Chris Jackson for NPR                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Given that history of exploitation, Tomson, the mayor of Davis, says he thinks the data center developer thought it could run roughshod over residents. But they got more than they bargained for, he says.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"This is a very educated community," Tomson says. "Many of the people here that have retired had very high-level scientific and technological careers elsewhere, and they bring that knowledge and expertise to bear on this situation."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Despite the organized opposition, &lt;a href="https://parsonsadvocate.com/news/pa-top-stories/headlines/commissioners-hear-constituents-on-ridgeline-project/" target="_blank"&gt;some residents have voiced support&lt;/a&gt;. Tucker County Sheriff Jake Kopec thinks much of the criticism amounts to fear-mongering. The landfill for Davis and Thomas blocks the view of the Ridgeline facility from those towns, he says. "I really believe that you would drive past it and not even know it's there."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Kopec acknowledges that the dark skies will be less dark. But he says the county has more immediate needs that the Ridgeline facility would help remedy, including better-paying jobs and tax revenue to fund essential public services. "We have no cops on after midnight in this county, but we serve a million-plus visitors a year," he notes.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;A vibrant arts scene&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Davis and Thomas — both with populations of roughly 600 people — are not only a base of operations for skiing, hiking, mountain biking and white water rafting, but they've also developed a lively arts and music scene.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"This area was just about written off," according to Tomson. "And what ended up happening was music and artists discovered the city of Thomas, and there was a beginning of a resurrection of the area."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;On a Sunday night in October well before the start of the ski season, there's a poetry reading at Creature in Thomas and a few doors down at the Purple Fiddle, a standing-room only performance by Driftwood, an Americana/folk rock band from Binghamton, N.Y.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Most of the hundred or so people in the bar are tourists like Adam Brooke, from Charlottesville, Va. He has been visiting the area for the past decade, taking in the mountains and the color of the fall leaves.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"We're mostly hikers," he says. "We just like getting out there on some of the lesser known trails and just enjoying nature for a bit."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Drawing hope from past environmental wins&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Despite the obstacles, opponents of the Ridgeline facility remain optimistic. They're buoyed by the &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/21/nx-s1-5927288/data-center-election-voters-ai" target="_blank"&gt;growing national opposition to data centers&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;In their own state, Gov. Morrisey — a strong advocate for data centers in the past — appears to be pumping the brakes somewhat, with a recently proposed 20-year &lt;a href="https://www.wvnews.com/news/wvnews/west-virginia-unveils-20-year-plan-for-responsible-data-center-development/article_4e051814-8b18-4fee-8a24-569c23fcc0ed.html" target="_blank"&gt;plan for "responsible" data center development&lt;/a&gt;. It's not much, Tucker United's Forrester says, but it's something.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;She also points to the region's past grassroots successes. "Tucker County does have a long history of fighting bad development proposals … but we've been successful in every single one of them."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-150636" class="bucketwrap image x-large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 4500;         --source-height: 3000;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F40%2Fcc%2F988f109349dea2bf017b82be0732%2Fwvdatacenter-22.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F40%2Fcc%2F988f109349dea2bf017b82be0732%2Fwvdatacenter-22.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F40%2Fcc%2F988f109349dea2bf017b82be0732%2Fwvdatacenter-22.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F40%2Fcc%2F988f109349dea2bf017b82be0732%2Fwvdatacenter-22.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F40%2Fcc%2F988f109349dea2bf017b82be0732%2Fwvdatacenter-22.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F40%2Fcc%2F988f109349dea2bf017b82be0732%2Fwvdatacenter-22.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F40%2Fcc%2F988f109349dea2bf017b82be0732%2Fwvdatacenter-22.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F40%2Fcc%2F988f109349dea2bf017b82be0732%2Fwvdatacenter-22.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F40%2Fcc%2F988f109349dea2bf017b82be0732%2Fwvdatacenter-22.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F40%2Fcc%2F988f109349dea2bf017b82be0732%2Fwvdatacenter-22.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F40%2Fcc%2F988f109349dea2bf017b82be0732%2Fwvdatacenter-22.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F40%2Fcc%2F988f109349dea2bf017b82be0732%2Fwvdatacenter-22.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F40%2Fcc%2F988f109349dea2bf017b82be0732%2Fwvdatacenter-22.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F40%2Fcc%2F988f109349dea2bf017b82be0732%2Fwvdatacenter-22.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F40%2Fcc%2F988f109349dea2bf017b82be0732%2Fwvdatacenter-22.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F40%2Fcc%2F988f109349dea2bf017b82be0732%2Fwvdatacenter-22.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F40%2Fcc%2F988f109349dea2bf017b82be0732%2Fwvdatacenter-22.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F40%2Fcc%2F988f109349dea2bf017b82be0732%2Fwvdatacenter-22.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F40%2Fcc%2F988f109349dea2bf017b82be0732%2Fwvdatacenter-22.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x3000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F40%2Fcc%2F988f109349dea2bf017b82be0732%2Fwvdatacenter-22.jpg" class="img" alt="A motorist drives past a “No Power Plant Data Center” sign in Canaan Valley, W.Va. (Chris Jackson/For NPR)" loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 A motorist drives past a "No Power Plant Data Center" sign in Canaan Valley, W.Va. (Chris Jackson/For NPR)                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Chris Jackson for NPR                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Forrester and others point to two major environmental fights in the 1970s: a &lt;a href="https://gettuckered.com/blog/history-of-canaan-valley/" target="_blank"&gt;proposed hydroelectric project&lt;/a&gt; that would have flooded Canaan Valley and part of Dolly Sods — a protected wilderness area now popular with hikers and skiers. A second, at Otter Creek, saw the West Virginia Highlands Conservancy successfully challenge plans for coal exploration and road construction in the Monongahela National Forest. Both were halted.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;Those victories are tempered by the region's darker past, too, she acknowledges.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"They're playing by the same playbook they've always played here," Forrester says. "People don't want to relive that history again, and they will fight every step of the way to make sure that doesn't happen."&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
